### API Gateway - route verification (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### EVERY request goes to port 8080. Start all services first (see docs/api-gateway-and-mcp-integration.md).
### Each request names the service that should answer it.

@gw = http://localhost:8080
@demoUserId = 7c9e6679-7425-40de-944b-e07fc1f90ae7

### 1. Gateway health
GET {{gw}}/actuator/health

### 2. All active routes - expect 10 routes (product-write-service, product-service,
#     stock-reservations-blocked, stock-service, order-service, user-service, rag-service,
#     mcp-client-api, mcp-client-ui, root-redirect)
GET {{gw}}/actuator/gateway/routes

### ===================== PRODUCTS =====================

### 3. GET -> product-service (Elasticsearch read side) - expect a page of products
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/products?q=gaming&size=3

> {% client.global.set("productId", response.body.content[0].id); %}

### 4. GET by id -> product-service - expect a product with "version"
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/products/{{productId}}

### 5. GET facets -> product-service
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/products/facets

### 6. POST -> product-write-service (MySQL write side) - expect 201
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/products
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{demoUserId}}

{
  "sku": "GW-TEST-001",
  "name": "Gateway Routing Test Keyboard",
  "description": "Mechanical keyboard used to verify gateway routing.",
  "brand": "TestBrand",
  "category": "accessories",
  "price": 79.00,
  "rating": 4.1,
  "tags": ["test", "keyboard"]
}

> {% client.global.set("writeProductId", response.body.id); %}

### 7. DELETE -> product-write-service - expect 204
DELETE {{gw}}/api/v1/products/{{writeProductId}}

### ===================== STOCK =====================

### 8. Availability -> stock-service - expect "available": true
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/stock/LAP-APL-001/availability?quantity=1

### 9. Low-stock report -> stock-service
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/stock?lowStockOnly=true

### 10. Reservations are INTERNAL - expect 403 from the gateway (never reaches stock-service)
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/stock/reservations
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "HACK-1", "items": [ { "sku": "LAP-APL-001", "quantity": 999 } ] }

### ===================== ORDERS =====================

### 11. Order-service catalogue copy -> order-service - expect "totalElements" >= 30
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/orders/catalog?size=3

### 12. Create an order -> order-service - expect 202 PENDING (watch the gateway log: user=...)
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json
X-User-Id: {{demoUserId}}

{
  "userId": "{{demoUserId}}",
  "items": [ { "sku": "AUD-APL-001", "quantity": 1 } ]
}

> {% client.global.set("gwOrderId", response.body.id); %}

### 13. Get it -> order-service - expect CONFIRMED after about a second
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/orders/{{gwOrderId}}

### 14. Orders of the user -> order-service
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/orders?userId={{demoUserId}}
X-User-Id: {{demoUserId}}

### ===================== USERS =====================

### 15. List users -> user-service
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/users?size=3

### ===================== RAG =====================

### 15b. Knowledge-base documents -> rag-service
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/rag/documents

### 15c. Retrieval -> rag-service
POST {{gw}}/api/v1/rag/search
Content-Type: application/json

{ "query": "return policy for opened headphones", "topK": 3 }

### ===================== CHAT =====================

### 16. Chat UI -> mcp-client - expect HTML
GET {{gw}}/chat/

### 17. Root -> 302 redirect to /chat/
GET {{gw}}/

### 18. Unknown path - expect 404 ProblemDetail FROM THE GATEWAY ("No API exists at this path.")
GET {{gw}}/api/v1/unknown
